<BaseLayout title="Motor Mounts" description="Motor mounts and swap kits for LS Hyundai Genesis Coupe builds.">
  <h1>Motor Mounts</h1>
  <p>
    Purpose-built kits (Sikky, ISR / Uniq-linked kits, LOJ, and others) place the engine for clearance, driveline angle, and header room.
    Universal LS mount brackets exist and can be cut to fit, but kit geometry usually saves time and mistakes.
  </p>

  <h2>Kit vs Universal</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sikky / ISR-style kits:</strong> Frequently mentioned on Reddit and Facebook for Genesis Coupe LS swaps.</li>
    <li><strong>LOJ:</strong> Sells Genesis Coupe-specific mounts, oil pan, and related hardware.</li>
    <li><strong>Universal plate-style mounts:</strong> Used on budget builds; expect to measure, cut, and weld or bolt carefully.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Related</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Transmission mount must match the gearbox you choose (T56, 4L60, 4L80, etc.).</li>
    <li>Engine position drives driveshaft length — mock up before ordering a shaft.</li>
    <li>BK1 vs BK2 front clearance affects how far forward you can sit the engine with a given accessory drive.</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
